      "side": 1,
      "message": "Replacing the `OutputFileProducer` interface for this module with the provider is only safe if everything that needs it can get the provider value.  Since `OutputFilesForModuleFromProvider` is skipped for non-`ModuleContext` callers and returns nil when called from the same module, don\u0027t you need the `OutputFileProducer` still as a fallback?\n\nAlternatively, can you handle those cases?  We talked about abstracting some of this away into `android.ModuleBase`, which could then be used to return the appropriate value without going through the provider.  So the module could call `ctx.SetOutputFiles(bpf.objs)`, which would temporarily store the values in ModuleBase, then `ModuleBase.GenerateBuildActions` would set the provider, and `OutputFilesForModuleFromProvider` could fall back to getting the values from `ModuleBase` when called on the current module.",
